<html><head><title>No Predetermined Result</title>
<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><h1 style="margin-bottom: 16px; font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; line-height: 1.4; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 32px;"><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 16pt; line-height: 24.7467px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">Welcome to the path of potential outcomes of a transdisciplinary education project. These outcomes are divided into:<o:p></o:p></font></span></p><ul><li style="text-indent: -18pt;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Symbol;">·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">Learning outcomes for participants: what do participants (primarily students) learn, and how does this contribute to their development?<o:p></o:p></span></font></li></ul><ul><li style="text-indent: -18pt;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Symbol;">·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">Additional benefits for participants: here, we outline outcomes that cannot be predetermined but are highly valuable. Think of stepping out of the comfort zone and allowing room for making mistakes.<o:p></o:p></span></font></li></ul><ul><li style="text-indent: -18pt;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Symbol;">·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">Visible (tangible) outcomes: such as knowledge acquisition and action-oriented results.<o:p></o:p></span></font></li></ul><ul><li style="text-indent: -18pt;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Symbol;">·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">Sustainability of impact: This section addresses how the impact can be made sustainable.</span></font></li></ul><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style="text-indent: -18pt;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><br></span></font></p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style="text-indent: -18pt;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><o:p></o:p></span></font></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000"><span style="font-weight: bolder;">Learning and personal development</span><o:p></o:p></font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">The powerful learning effects of transdisciplinary collaboration are a significant result of such cooperation. Participants, from students to professionals, not only develop knowledge and skills but might also transform their values. This process of personal and professional growth of individuals, is a crucial step towards effectively tackling complex problems and promoting a sustainable future.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000"><span style="font-weight: bolder;">Professional development</span><o:p></o:p></font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">As previously mentioned: "the journey, not the destination, is important in transdisciplinary education." The development of professional competencies and the inner development of each team member are at least as important as the final product. All participants have worked on their personal and professional development. By addressing a complex problem from various perspectives, both interdisciplinary and cross-sectoral, individuals learn about their own expertise through the reflections of others and gain insights into the experiences and expertise of others. As explained in the page&nbsp;<i>What to Learn</i>, significant inner development can be expected in the domains being, thinking, relating, collaborating, and acting (<a href="https://innerdevelopmentgoals.org/">Inner Development Goals</a>).<o:p></o:p></font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000"><span style="font-weight: bolder;">Intrinsic values</span><o:p></o:p></font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">Another transformation can occur within the&nbsp;<i>values</i>&nbsp;that participants hold dear. By being exposed to different and new perspectives on relevant topics, your values can transform. For instance, awareness may increase when working on complex issues like the clothing industry. By gaining knowledge and perspectives, participants may change their personal choices and the lens through which they view the world.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">For example, business innovation student who collaborated with partners at De Kleine Aarde, an ecological centre affiliated with Avans University of Applied Sciences (NL, on a project around meat production, reported that their views on meat consumption had changed. They became more aware of the holistic consequences of meat production.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000"><span style="font-weight: bolder;">Education for the future</span><o:p></o:p></font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">The invisible outcomes of a transdisciplinary project can extend beyond the individual level. In democratic countries like the Netherlands, citizens need to have a strong sense of value to participate in democracy. Transdisciplinary education, which crosses boundaries and combines multiple perspectives, can play an active role in this field of politics (Hoggan &amp; Hoggan-Kloubert, 2023).</font></span></p></h1></body></html>